  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nRidging shifts to the east this weekend as as a trough over the \nwestern US lifts into the northern Plains. This will allow for \nsouthwesterly flow aloft to reestablish and bring the potential for \nsome weak disturbances to move over the area. Overall, the weekend \nhas trended drier with only very low and rather isolated \nprecipitation chances mainly over the southern Edwards Plateau and \nHill Country during this time. The vast majority of the area will \nexperience a rather quiet and warm weekend.\n\nEarly next week, better moisture and higher precipitable water \nvalues return over the area bringing more widespread, but still low, \nrain chances to the region. Guidance suggests Tuesday may have our \n\"best\" chances for rain in the region, but nothing overtly organized \nis seen bringing a fair bit of uncertainty to the forecast during \nthis early to mid-week timeframe. Temperatures remain near or \nslightly above seasonable values in the long-term.",
